      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}={b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=-3{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2}+2{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-5{b}_{2}+2{b}_{3}+4{b}_{1} \\\\  & =5(-{b}_{2})+2{b}_{3}-4(-{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(-2{b}_{2})+2{c}_{2}-\\frac{4}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
